QGC WPL 110
# ============================================================================
# AIRSPEED FAILURE BEHAVIOR MISSION v1
# Purpose:
#   Purpose-built mission for the airspeed_failure_behavior lane. It is NOT the
#   old airspeed_validation_mission (which existed for airspeed INTEGRATION
#   testing). This mission is designed for fault-injection behavior
#   characterization: inject one airspeed fault at a fixed, repeatable point and
#   observe the aircraft response over a long straight cruise leg, then a
#   reciprocal leg, then RTL.
#
# Design decisions (see governance/runbooks/features/airspeed_failure_behavior/
# design_adrs.md, "ADR (Proposed): Airspeed Failure Mission Design"):
#   - Cruise altitude 100 m AGL (high vertical margin so altitude loss / TECS
#     fighting a bad airspeed is observable before terrain).
#   - 800 m measurement legs (~80 s East headwind, ~40 s West tailwind).
#   - Injection fires on ENTERING seq 4 (MISSION_CURRENT.seq==4, first edge):
#     the aircraft has settled on seq 3 and begins the straight 800 m East
#     headwind measurement leg toward WP4, giving ~800 m of clean post-injection
#     cruise before the seq 5 turn, plus the full reciprocal West leg.
#   - Mission ends in RTL (seq 9). There is NO landing sequence. Completion =
#     front-half progress + both measurement legs + RTL reached and stabilized.
#
# World assumptions:
#   - Home: lat=-35.363262, lon=149.165237
#   - Fixed reference wind (Gazebo world ENU): x=-5, y=0, z=0 m/s
#     (-X => wind blowing West => headwind on the Eastbound leg, tailwind West).
#   - ENU axes: +X East, +Y North. Aircraft starts facing East, takes off into
#     the wind. CONFIRM the wind sign on the smoke build (see reference-wind ADR).
#
# Commanded cruise: DO_CHANGE_SPEED = 15 m/s (inside the conservative 14/22
#   AIRSPEED envelope of config/overlays/plane_airspeed.parm).
#
# Expected steady-state (healthy_reference, fixed -5,0,0 wind):
#   - East measurement leg (WP3 -> WP4, headwind):  ARSP ~15, GPS ~10, ARSP-GPS ~+5
#   - West measurement leg (WP6 -> WP7, tailwind):   ARSP ~15, GPS ~20, ARSP-GPS ~-5
#   The +5/-5 sign flip is the per-attempt wind/observability sanity check.
#
# Injection point: seq 4. Ignore takeoff transient and turn segments for
#   steady-state interpretation.
# ============================================================================

# Home
0	1	0	16	0	0	0	0	-35.3632620	149.1652370	584.00	1

# WP1: TAKEOFF East, climb to 100 m AGL
1	0	3	22	15.0	0	0	0	-35.3632620	149.1668924	100.00	1

# WP2: Command target airspeed = 15 m/s
# MAV_CMD_DO_CHANGE_SPEED (178): param1=0 (airspeed), param2=15
2	0	0	178	0	15.0	0	0	0	0	0	1

# WP3: Eastbound settle leg start, 300 m East of home (stabilize cruise)
3	0	3	16	0	0	0	0	-35.3632620	149.1685416	100.00	1

# WP4: Eastbound MEASUREMENT leg end, 1100 m East of home (800 m measurement leg)
# INJECTION POINT: fault is injected on ENTERING seq 4 (start of WP3->WP4 leg).
4	0	3	16	0	0	0	0	-35.3632620	149.1773540	100.00	1

# WP5: North offset for reciprocal turn, 150 m North / 1100 m East
5	0	3	16	0	0	0	0	-35.3619145	149.1773540	100.00	1

# WP6: Westbound MEASUREMENT leg start, 150 m North / 1100 m East
6	0	3	16	0	0	0	0	-35.3619145	149.1773540	100.00	1

# WP7: Westbound MEASUREMENT leg end, 150 m North / 300 m East (800 m measurement leg)
7	0	3	16	0	0	0	0	-35.3619145	149.1685416	100.00	1

# WP8: Return toward home, 150 m North of home
8	0	3	16	0	0	0	0	-35.3619145	149.1652370	100.00	1

# WP9: RETURN TO LAUNCH. Mission ends here; no landing sequence.
# MAV_CMD_NAV_RETURN_TO_LAUNCH (20). Completion = RTL reached and stabilized.
9	0	3	20	0	0	0	0	0	0	0	1
